################################################################################
# 
# REVISED ANALYSIS CODE
#
# Reviewer-driven revisions:
#
# AE-1 / R1-1:
#   Do NOT apply GARCH directly to fitted conditional means.
#   GARCH is applied to standardized count innovations.
#
# AE-2 / R1-2:
#   Do NOT multiply fitted means by simulated copula values.
#   Copula models cross-sectional spatial dependence separately from
#   the marginal count model.
#
# AE-3 / R1-3:
#   Add chronological temporal out-of-sample validation against a
#   non-spatial benchmark.
#
# AE-3 / R1-3:
#   Compare spatially informed and non-spatial volatility forecasting
#   using the same marginal count model and standardized innovations.
#
# R2-1:
#   Consider Poisson, Negative Binomial, and zero-inflated specifications.
#
# R2-2:
#   Explicitly examine zero counts, temporal variation, spatial variation,
#   and the empirical mean-variance relationship.
#
# R2-3:
#   Zero-inflated Poisson/NB specifications are included as optional
#   competing marginal models when supported by the data.
#
# R2-4:
#   Clustering is based primarily on full volatility trajectories rather
#   than only scalar average volatility.
#
# R2-5:
#   Dynamic Time Warping (DTW) is included as a clustering sensitivity
#   analysis.
#
# R2-6:
#   Cluster membership is interpreted as similarity in statistical
#   volatility behavior, NOT direct geographic transmission.
#
# GENERAL:
#   The revised analysis separates:
#
#   Count model
#       |
#       +--> Conditional mean
#       |
#       +--> Standardized count innovations
#                    |
#                    +--> GARCH conditional volatility
#
#   Temporal mean trajectories
#       |
#       +--> B-spline smoothing
#       +--> FPCA
#
#   Cross-location innovations
#       |
#       +--> Copula dependence
#
################################################################################

